#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Build an indexed bible from the source library's tracked verse text.

`mass-propers --bible <id>` looks a passage up by the exact reference string a
calendar prints, so an index cannot be a whole bible: the key space is the set
of references the calendars actually make, not a book/chapter/verse tree. This
tool walks every calendar, resolves each citation against the per-book verse
files registered under the edition in `src/sources/works/`, and writes the
resulting `passages` map.

The verse text is never re-downloaded. It comes from the tracked artifacts of
the registered edition, so a rebuild is offline, deterministic, and diffable
against the same bytes the source library already verified.
"""
