# A psalm reference resolves against a psalter, and the Latin psalters differ in
# wording where they agree in numbering, so numbering alone cannot identify the
# text. Two editions differing only in recension would otherwise be
# indistinguishable, and a near-miss reads as a match. `masoretic` is not a
# recension of the Latin psalter at all; it names the Hebrew text a psalter
# Englished from the Hebrew witnesses, and it is here because calling such a
# psalter `iuxta-hebraeos` would assert Jerome's third Latin psalter, which it
# is not.
